{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Plan-review v1 returned BLOCK (G6) — remediated, re-review launched\n\n**Blocking finding (G6, critical):** `_NEVER_COUNTED_KINDS` was a SECOND hand-maintained enumeration of the is_issue=False decisions, which actually live at independent production sites (the `_tracker_health` pairs, `_DIRTY_LINE_SPECS`, and inline scan flags). A future is_issue=False kind added at a production site would update the exit code but NOT the constant — silently reintroducing the very count-disagreement being fixed.\n\n**Remediation (in-scope hardening of the approved fix, no new design):**\n- **Single-sourced** the tracker-dirty portion: `_NEVER_COUNTED_TRACKER_DIRTY_KINDS` is now DERIVED from `_DIRTY_LINE_SPECS` (`{kind for (…,counted) in specs if not counted}`), so a future `counted=False` dirty class flows in automatically — that whole site can no longer drift.\n- The three inline scan/health kinds (`push_pending`, `status_fork_resolved`, `warn`) are an explicit `_NEVER_COUNTED_SCAN_KINDS`; each production site now carries a pointer comment back to the constant (the reviewer's fallback 'note' remedy).\n- **Drift-guard tests** added to test_fsck_issue_count_29c3.py: (a) round-trip asserting the derived dirty set == the `counted=False` specs and no `counted=True` class leaks in; (b) the constant is exactly the union of its two documented components; (c) a behavioural invariant that the counted subset == the exit-code tally across a payload mixing every never-counted kind. A new is_issue=False kind that forgets the constant now fails a test.\n\n**Advisories also addressed:** T4 (added an explicit expand-contract / back-out reversibility paragraph to the Consumer assessment) and P6 (split the compound acceptance criteria into independently-verifiable lines).\n\nDescription + file-impact updated (12 paths). Re-running `review-plan`. Test count: 14 pass in the held-out file (11 original + 3 drift guards)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787957076807826001,"uuid":"2fd66169-680a-44bc-984e-ef4f39155c03"}